<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # What Are the Jobs of the Future? – Lesson # 1</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0;"><em>Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</em></p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 1</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Listening</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 10th Grade (CEFR: B1.1)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Dream Jobs</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> What Are the Jobs of the Future?</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Listening: Receptive: Follow detailed oral instructions in class. Interactive: Interpret and relay information in pair and group discussions.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Listening: Can follow instructions from a career planning workshop (e.g., "I should study computer science and learn programming languages.")<br>Can interpret key details in a class discussion about future jobs and relay that information accurately during pair or group work (e.g., "They said that jobs in AI will need skills like data analysis and programming.").<br>Can identify key points from a group discussion on career goals, taking notes and summarizing information (e.g., "What career paths might emerge due to automation, and what skills are required?").</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher starts by showing images of various modern and innovative technologies (e.g., AI robots, virtual reality headsets, self-driving cars). Students listen to short, descriptive phrases about each image, and then in pairs, quickly discuss what kind of jobs these technologies might create or replace. The teacher asks, "What future jobs will these technologies bring?" or "Which jobs may disappear due to automation?"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher introduces key vocabulary related to future jobs and skills by orally presenting sentences and definitions. For example: "<b>Automation</b> will change many industries." (automation, change, industries). "New <b>skills</b> will be in high <b>demand</b>." (skills, demand). "Some jobs will <b>evolve</b>, requiring greater <b>adaptability</b>." (evolve, adaptability). The teacher models the pronunciation of /dʒ/ in "change" and /ʒ/ in "vision" (e.g., "technological vision") and the stress in "automation," "advancement," and "adaptability."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If a job is 'in demand,' does that mean many people want it or many companies need it?" (Expected answer: Many companies need it.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When a job 'evolves,' does it stay the same or does it gradually change?" (Expected answer: It gradually changes.)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">[Date] <br> [5-7 min]</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Dream Jobs".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short audio excerpt (approx. 2 minutes) from a career planning podcast titled "Navigating the Future Workforce," discussing emerging jobs in AI, technology, and remote work, and the skills required for them. It includes predictions using future simple and continuous, and modals of possibility.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Interpret and relay information in pair and group discussions.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ol>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>First Listening (Gist):</b> The teacher instructs students to listen for the main idea. "What is the podcast mainly about?" (e.g., future employment opportunities, changing job market, career advancement).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Second Listening (Detailed):</b> The teacher provides a worksheet with True/False statements or a matching activity. Students listen again to identify specific details.
                        <ul>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example True/False: "Jobs in artificial intelligence will mainly require physical strength." (False)</li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Example Matching: Match future jobs (e.g., "AI ethicist") with required skills (e.g., "critical thinking").</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                </ol>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">[Date] <br> [10-12 min]</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Listening.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Listening for key vocabulary (e.g., 'automation,' 'AI,' 'remote work,' 'adaptability,' 'innovation,' 'demand,' 'evolve,' 'acquire,' 'require') and grammatical structures (Future simple for prediction, Future continuous for long-term goals, Modals for possibilities).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Gap-Fill Listening:</b> Students receive a transcript of the audio with 8-10 target vocabulary words removed (e.g., 'future,' 'skills,' 'demand,' 'AI,' 'advancement,' 'adaptability,' 'evolve,' 'innovate'). The teacher plays the audio again, and students fill in the blanks. After listening, they check answers in pairs. (Focus: Receptive listening for specific words, including stress practice for words like "employment," "artificial intelligence").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Sentence Transformation Listening:</b> The teacher presents a list of sentences heard in the audio (e.g., "People will work more from home.") and asks students to listen again and identify if the sentence uses Future Simple, Future Continuous, or a Modal for possibility. Then, students are given prompts to transform sentences, for instance, changing "New careers will emerge" to a statement using a modal of possibility: "New careers may emerge." The teacher guides pronunciation practice for /dʒ/ in "emerge."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Listen and Summarize Key Phrases:</b> In pairs, students listen to short snippets (15-20 seconds) from the podcast. After each snippet, one student quickly summarizes the key prediction or skill mentioned, while the partner checks for accuracy and correct use of target vocabulary (e.g., "The speaker said that jobs in the <b>future</b> will <b>require</b> advanced <b>skills</b> in <b>technology</b>."). They also ensure correct pronunciation of words like "technological" and "advancement."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">[Date] <br> [12-15 min]</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Dream Jobs".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Group Discussion & Relay</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students form small groups (3-4 students). The teacher presents 3-4 different short audio clips (30-45 seconds each) – each clip detailing a distinct emerging career path or a specific skill in demand for the future job market (e.g., "Data Ethics Specialist," "Sustainable Energy Engineer," "AI Prompt Engineer").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Each group listens to ALL clips. After listening, groups discuss: "What careers do you think will be in demand based on what you heard?", "What skills will be required for these jobs?", and "What opportunities may arise from these changes?". Students are encouraged to use future simple, future continuous, and modals (e.g., "In ten years, people will be developing new AI solutions," "These jobs may require strong analytical skills").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">After the group discussion, one student from each group orally relays the main points of their discussion to another group, or to the whole class, explaining personal career goals and insights. For example, "They said that jobs in AI will need skills like data analysis and programming. I will be an engineer and will work on innovative projects." The teacher reminds students to adapt their tone and formality (sociolinguistic competence) when addressing peers vs. the whole class.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">This task focuses on active listening, interpreting information, and accurately relaying it, ensuring all target vocabulary and grammar are used in a meaningful context.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">[Date] <br> [12-15 min]</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist focusing on listening comprehension and relaying information. Peer assessment during group relay activity.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students collectively create a mind map or a short bullet-point summary on the board or on individual mini-whiteboards titled "Skills for Future Jobs," incorporating at least 5 new vocabulary words and 2 future tense predictions they heard during the entire lesson.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Intelligible pronunciation:</b> Clear articulation of target vocabulary (e.g., "automation," "advancement," "adaptability," "employment," "artificial intelligence," "remote work").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of target vocabulary:</b> Accurate and relevant inclusion of words like 'jobs,' 'skills,' 'future,' 'demand,' 'AI,' 'remote work,' 'adaptability.'</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarity and Accuracy:</b> Ability to clearly interpret and relay information from listened content and group discussions.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Collaboration:</b> Active participation in group discussions and constructive contribution to the summary.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer the following questions individually:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What is one job of the future that you learned about today, and what skill does it require?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How confident are you in understanding detailed instructions in English now (1-5 scale)?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">[Date] <br> [5-7 min]</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was challenging about listening to predictions about future jobs, and how did I overcome it?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What new vocabulary or phrase did I find most useful for discussing career goals?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in helping students follow detailed oral instructions and interpret information? (e.g., audio clips with varied speakers, clear instructions, visual aids).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for next time, especially concerning the length or complexity of audio input, or supporting students in relaying information accurately? (e.g., provide a scaffolded note-taking guide).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> This lesson introduced core vocabulary and concepts about future jobs through listening. The next lesson (Lesson 2: Reading Comprehension) will use a text containing the same vocabulary and grammatical structures to deepen understanding and provide context for these terms, allowing students to read about the future job market.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">[Date] <br> [3-4 min]</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>